            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic floor therapies in chronic pelvic pain syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>304-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11934-011-0197-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic pelvic pain syndrome is a poorly understood clinical entity associated with urinary symptoms, pelvic floor dysfunction, and multisystem disorders. Treatment of pelvic floor dysfunction is difficult and often frustrating for the patient as well as for the involved physician. The purpose of this review is to update clinicians on the latest research for the treatment of pelvic floor dysfunction in relation to chronic pelvic pain syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
